    [746] = {
        {11012, "Cho'war the Pillager", [[ King Molgar and his champions are the mightiest ogres in Netherstorm; they form Gruul's guard, protecting his lair. Each of these champions possesses unique abilities, and their combined might can only be surpassed by Gruul's own iron grip. ]], 0.550255, 0.570769, 2, 864, 11981, 746, 8, 0, 0},
        {11013, "Gruul the Dragonkiller", [[ This gigantic gronn made a name for himself as the Dragonkiller during the battle against Deathwing's black dragonflight, who wished to hide her brood's eggs in Blade's Edge Mountains. Dwelling in the immense cavern of Gruul's Lair, he alone represents a terrifying threat to any non-ogre in Blade's Edge Mountains. ]], 0.249486, 0.283077, 2, 864, 11960, 746, 8, 0, 1},
        {1564, "Cho'war the Pillager", [[ King Molgar and his champions are the mightiest ogres in Netherstorm; they form Gruul's guard, protecting his lair. Each of these champions possesses unique abilities, and their combined might can only be surpassed by Gruul's own iron grip. ]], 0.550255, 0.570769, 1, 864, 11981, 746, 2, 0, 0},
        {1565, "Gruul the Dragonkiller", [[ This gigantic gronn made a name for himself as the Dragonkiller during the battle against Deathwing's black dragonflight, who wished to hide her brood's eggs in Blade's Edge Mountains. Dwelling in the immense cavern of Gruul's Lair, he alone represents a terrifying threat to any non-ogre in Blade's Edge Mountains. ]], 0.199486, 0.283077, 1, 864, 11960, 746, 2, 0, 1},
    },
    [747] = {
        {11014, "Magtheridon", [[ Illidan helped Akama defeat the demons and orcs of Magtheridon, and together, they stormed the Hellfire Citadel. Magtheridon eventually fell beneath Illidan's blows. Or so it was believed... When Illidan crushed Magtheridon, the pit lord hovered between life and death, but understanding this, Illidan chose to let him live. He ordered his servants to hide Magtheridon's body in a cave, in order to use his fel blood to sustain the demonic power of the orcs. Illidan's servants drain most of the demon's blood daily, keeping him in a comatose state. Should Magtheridon ever awaken, he would likely try to reclaim Zangarmarsh... ]], 0.691795, 0.743077, 1, 865, 11919, 747, 8, 0, 0},
        {1566, "Magtheridon", [[ Illidan helped Akama defeat the demons and orcs of Magtheridon, and together, they stormed the Hellfire Citadel. Magtheridon eventually fell beneath Illidan's blows. Or so it was believed... When Illidan crushed Magtheridon, the pit lord hovered between life and death, but understanding this, Illidan chose to let him live. He ordered his servants to hide Magtheridon's body in a cave, in order to use his fel blood to sustain the demonic power of the orcs. Illidan's servants drain most of the demon's blood daily, keeping him in a comatose state. Should Magtheridon ever awaken, he would likely try to reclaim Zangarmarsh... ]], 0.691795, 0.743077, 1, 865, 11919, 747, 2, 0, 0},
    },
    [748] = {
        {1567, "Hydross the Unstable", [[ A huge water elemental dwells in the Coilfang Reservoir's Serpentshrine, purifying itself of the corruption that struck it, like much of the elementals of Zangarmarsh, and helping the younger elementals purify themselves as well. But despite all the naga's efforts, Hydross remains unstable, and as soon as it leaves the range of the machines built by the naga, the poison overtakes it once more. ]], 0.363590, 0.847692, 1, 862, 700, 748, 2, 0, 0},
        {1568, "The Lurker Below", [[ Astonishing creatures inhabit Zangarmarsh, and not all of them live on the surface. Deep within Serpentshrine Cavern lives a strange creature, similar to the krakens that dwell in the northern seas of Azeroth: the Lurker Below. Anyone who disturbs this strange body of water, where the naga feed the Lurker, will make a discovery that is, to say the least... unusual. ]], 0.402564, 0.581538, 1, 862, 711, 748, 2, 0, 1},
        {1569, "Leotheras the Blind", [[ Leotheras was one of five blood elves whom Illidan took under his wing to make demon hunters. But the path of the demon hunter is not for the faint of heart, and three of the five lost their lives in the process. A far darker fate awaited Leotheras, weak of spirit. After undergoing the ritual and gaining an inner demon, Leotheras failed to keep control of it and sank into madness. The spellweavers of Serpentshrine Cavern keep him captive, trying to restore his sanity, but in vain, for in Leotheras's mind two voices now forever echo, his own and the demon's. ]], 0.417949, 0.255385, 1, 862, 722, 748, 2, 0, 2},
        {1570, "Fathom-Lord Karathress", [[ Karathress commands Lady Vashj's personal guard. An experienced warrior and merciless commander, Karathress has chosen three guards endowed with unique abilities. Together, they form the last line of defense of Serpentshrine Cavern and remain undefeated, for Karathress holds a secret only discovered at the threshold of death. ]], 0.504103, 0.176924, 1, 862, 738, 748, 2, 0, 3},
        {1571, "Morogrim Tidewalker", [[ Sea giants, powerful, malevolent, and generally not very bright, are humanoids found on the forgotten islands of Azeroth, usually hostile to everyone and everything. Morogrim Tidewalker is an exception to this rule. It is unknown how the naga convinced this giant to settle in Serpentshrine Cavern, but he now resides here, surrounded by a horde of murlocs who obey him. ]], 0.596410, 0.260001, 1, 862, 769, 748, 2, 0, 4},
        {1572, "Lady Vashj", [[ Azshara's chief servant, transformed into a naga like her mistress, she was sent to aid Illidan on his journey to destroy the Frozen Throne. Though her new lord did not succeed, Lady Vashj followed him to Zangarmarsh, where Illidan and his troops hastily began fortifying their positions in anticipation of the Legion's wrath. This powerful sea witch now rules Serpentshrine Cavern and is a formidable opponent, even for the most seasoned warriors. ]], 0.722563, 0.589231, 1, 862, 777, 748, 2, 0, 5},
        {11650, "Hydross the Unstable", [[ A huge water elemental dwells in the Coilfang Reservoir's Serpentshrine, purifying itself of the corruption that struck it, like much of the elementals of Zangarmarsh, and helping the younger elementals purify themselves as well. But despite all the naga's efforts, Hydross remains unstable, and as soon as it leaves the range of the machines built by the naga, the poison overtakes it once more. ]], 0.359000, 0.799000, 2, 862, 20930, 748, 8, 0, 0},
        {11651, "Gore'lac", [[ At the bottom of the reservoir, within the mysterious branching underground caves, fused into the rock, lives a creature of monstrous size made of spines, venom, and chitin, known as Gore'lac. The oldest creature of Coilfang, whose mind far exceeds the level of the primitive creatures inhabiting the reservoir. Only rarely, tempted by irresistible prey, does this giant crab leave its lair and rise to the surface to drag its food into the deep waters. Its appearance awakens other predatory creatures of the underwater world, but several of Lady Vashj's trusted overseers make sure Gore'lac does not leave the depths for too long.
Will a skilled fisherman, armed with a sturdy enough rod, be found to pull this ancient crab from the depths? ]], 0.403000, 0.589000, 2, 862, 20998, 748, 8, 0, 1},
        {11652, "Leotheras the Blind", [[ Leotheras was one of five blood elves whom Illidan took under his wing to make demon hunters. But the path of the demon hunter is not for the faint of heart, and three of the five lost their lives in the process. A far darker fate awaited Leotheras, weak of spirit. After undergoing the ritual and gaining an inner demon, Leotheras failed to keep control of it and sank into madness. The spellweavers of Serpentshrine Cavern keep him captive, trying to restore his sanity, but in vain, for in Leotheras's mind two voices now forever echo, his own and the demon's. ]], 0.417949, 0.255385, 2, 862, 20952, 748, 8, 0, 2},
        {11653, "Fathom-Lord Karathress", [[ Karathress commands Lady Vashj's personal guard. An experienced warrior and merciless commander, Karathress has chosen three guards endowed with unique abilities. Together, they form the last line of defense of Serpentshrine Cavern and remain undefeated, for Karathress holds a secret only discovered at the threshold of death. ]], 0.504103, 0.176924, 2, 862, 21019, 748, 8, 0, 3},
        {11654, "Morogrim Tidewalker", [[ Sea giants, powerful, malevolent, and generally not very bright, are humanoids found on the forgotten islands of Azeroth, usually hostile to everyone and everything. Morogrim Tidewalker is an exception to this rule. It is unknown how the naga convinced this giant to settle in Serpentshrine Cavern, but he now resides here, surrounded by a horde of murlocs who obey him. ]], 0.596410, 0.260001, 2, 862, 21080, 748, 8, 0, 4},
        {11655, "Lady Vashj", [[ Azshara's chief servant, transformed into a naga like her mistress, she was sent to aid Illidan on his journey to destroy the Frozen Throne. Though her new lord did not succeed, Lady Vashj followed him to Zangarmarsh, where Illidan and his troops hastily began fortifying their positions in anticipation of the Legion's wrath. This powerful sea witch now rules Serpentshrine Cavern and is a formidable opponent, even for the most seasoned warriors. ]], 0.722563, 0.589231, 2, 862, 21113, 748, 8, 0, 5},
    },
    [749] = {
        {1573, "Al'ar", [[ This phoenix, Kael'thas's traveling companion and faithful familiar, Al'ar has grown considerably in power since the day he and Kael'thas first met. Today, he and his offspring serve their master, residing in the Tempest Keep. ]], 0.501026, 0.587692, 1, 782, 806, 749, 2, 0, 0},
        {1574, "Void Reaver", [[ This engine of corruption, built by the demons of the Burning Legion in service to Kael'thas and refined by blood elf engineers, uses its immense physical strength and the power of arcane magic to guard the left wing of the Tempest Keep. ]], 0.264075, 0.490686, 1, 782, 819, 749, 2, 0, 1},
        {1575, "Grand Astromancer Solarian", [[ A chief astrologer must possess a keen mind, a deep knowledge of arcane magic, and the ability to gaze into the abyss without losing her sanity. Solarian performs her duties admirably under Kael'thas's direction, and over time, her abilities have been enriched by knowledge drawn from the Twisting Nether. Need it be said that this knowledge will be put to use in battle when needed? ]], 0.740000, 0.489230, 1, 782, 823, 749, 2, 0, 2},
        {1576, "Kael'thas Sunstrider", [[ Ruler of the blood elves, last prince of his people, Kael'thas Sunstrider has seized the Tempest Keep and turned it into his stronghold, with a single goal: to seize control of the chaotic energies of the Twisting Nether and turn them into a power capable of annihilating any enemy, thereby helping his people quench their thirst for magic. ]], 0.500999, 0.138461, 1, 782, 836, 749, 2, 0, 3},
        {11573, "Al'ar", [[ This phoenix, Kael'thas's traveling companion and faithful familiar, Al'ar has grown considerably in power since the day he and Kael'thas first met. Today, he and his offspring serve their master, residing in the Tempest Keep. ]], 0.501026, 0.587692, 1, 782, 1500, 749, 8, 0, 0},
        {11574, "Void Reaver", [[ This engine of corruption, built by the demons of the Burning Legion in service to Kael'thas and refined by blood elf engineers, uses its immense physical strength and the power of arcane magic to guard the left wing of the Tempest Keep. ]], 0.264075, 0.490686, 1, 782, 1539, 749, 8, 0, 1},
        {11575, "Grand Astromancer Solarian", [[ A chief astrologer must possess a keen mind, a deep knowledge of arcane magic, and the ability to gaze into the abyss without losing her sanity. Solarian performs her duties admirably under Kael'thas's direction, and over time, her abilities have been enriched by knowledge drawn from the Twisting Nether. Need it be said that this knowledge will be put to use in battle when needed? ]], 0.740000, 0.489230, 1, 782, 1559, 749, 8, 0, 2},
        {11576, "Kael'thas Sunstrider", [[ Ruler of the blood elves, last prince of his people, Kael'thas Sunstrider has seized the Tempest Keep and turned it into his stronghold, with a single goal: to seize control of the chaotic energies of the Twisting Nether and turn them into a power capable of annihilating any enemy, thereby helping his people quench their thirst for magic. ]], 0.500999, 0.138461, 1, 782, 1604, 749, 8, 0, 3},
    },
    [753] = {
        {1597, "Ironhand", [[ The weakest of the vault's guardians, Ironhand the Stone Keeper is an immense stone giant who wields the powers of earth. ]], 0.493350, 0.168738, 1, 532, 11475, 753, 3, 0, 0},
        {1598, "Emalon the Storm Watcher", [[ Emalon the Storm Keeper is a giant endowed with the powers of the storm. He and his storm summoners guard Ironhand's Vault. ]], 0.627193, 0.553059, 1, 532, 11489, 753, 3, 0, 1},
        {1599, "Koralon the Flame Watcher", [[ Koralon the Fire Keeper is one of the guardians of Ironhand's Vault, a mighty stone giant endowed with the powers of fire. ]], 0.363289, 0.551625, 1, 532, 11479, 753, 3, 0, 2},
        {1600, "Toravon the Ice Watcher", [[ Toravon the Ice Keeper is the mightiest of the guardians of Ironhand's Vault, a stone giant endowed with the powers of ice. ]], 0.627151, 0.363767, 1, 532, 11484, 753, 3, 0, 3},
    },
    [754] = {
        {1601, "Anub'Rekhan", [[ Anub'Rekhan is one of the nerubian lords, guardian of the Arachnid Quarter at Naxxramas. ]], 0.306925, 0.469885, 2, 535, 11497, 754, 3, 0, 0},
        {1602, "Grand Widow Faerlina", [[ Once a talented alchemist, Faerlina is today one of the highest-ranking figures of the Cult of the Damned. Residing in the Arachnid Quarter at Naxxramas, she teaches the dark arts to her followers. ]], 0.441725, 0.360899, 2, 535, 11504, 754, 3, 0, 1},
        {1603, "Maexxna", [[ This giant spider has spun her web in one of the chambers of the Arachnid Quarter at Naxxramas. Object of Faerlina's and her cult's veneration, Maexxna increases the number of her offspring every day, keeping her venom as deadly as ever. ]], 0.686466, 0.152964, 2, 535, 11511, 754, 3, 0, 2},
        {1604, "Noth the Plaguebringer", [[ Just as Arthas answered the Lich King's call, Noth in his time joined the Scourge in search of power and might. However, during the Third War, Noth began to doubt his actions, and the Lich King, without hesitation, froze the heart in his chest. Since then, Noth knows neither doubt nor mercy, and only death can now stop him. ]], 0.346122, 0.564531, 4, 535, 11518, 754, 3, 0, 3},
        {1605, "Heigan the Unclean", [[ Heigan the Unclean, one of the necromancers who devoted himself intensely to the study and direct manipulation of the destructive plague, resides at Naxxramas, where he perfects and develops this new form of battle sorcery. His arsenal includes destructive spells, weakening curses, and he no doubt still has a few tricks in reserve. ]], 0.498172, 0.456978, 4, 535, 11525, 754, 3, 0, 4},
        {1606, "Loatheb", [[ Spore stragglers are extremely interesting creatures, born of the swamps. But Loatheb is unique, even among them. Strange mutations mean his mere presence spreads a necrotic aura that prevents any form of healing.
It did not take long before the Cult of the Damned took an interest in him, and Loatheb now resides in the Plague Quarter at Naxxramas. ]], 0.760165, 0.283523, 4, 535, 11530, 754, 3, 0, 5},
        {1607, "Instructor Razuvious", [[ One of the old death knights who remained loyal to the Lich King, even after the Ebon Blade knights' revolt. He now trains a new generation of death knights in the Military Quarter of Naxxramas. ]], 0.427469, 0.459909, 3, 535, 11537, 754, 3, 0, 6},
        {1608, "Gothik the Harvester", [[ Gothik the Harvester is an expert in necromancy and dark magic, one of the few necromancers capable of raising not only the body but also the soul, turning the deceased into spectral warriors. After the Ebon Blade knights' revolt, he can be found in the Military Quarter of Naxxramas, training novices in the art of dark magic. ]], 0.675078, 0.596142, 3, 535, 11545, 754, 3, 0, 7},
        {1609, "Baron Rivendare", [[ The most powerful death knights of Naxxramas are the four horsemen. They represent the pinnacle of Kel'Thuzad's guard. The first, Thane Korth'azz, holds the power of flame. The next, Lady Blaumeux, calls upon the power of shadow, drawing the souls of the living into an insatiable embrace. Sir Zeliek, a loyal paladin in life, is so strong in his faith that even with what little power remains to him, the holy Light still answers his call, striking his enemies in battle. The last death knight, Lord Mograine, was the finest warrior the death knights have ever known. However, after the events surrounding Azeroth, he vanished without a trace. Kel'Thuzad appointed Baron Rivendare to replace him. ]], 0.301273, 0.768225, 3, 535, 11606, 754, 3, 0, 8},
        {1610, "Patchwerk", [[ Patchwerk wants to play!
One of the most monstrous creations ever made by the Scourge. Having survived the Ebon Blade knights' revolt, Patchwerk proudly calls himself the 'Embodiment of War.' He now guards the corridors of the Abomination Quarter at Naxxramas. ]], 0.541192, 0.416887, 1, 535, 11622, 754, 3, 0, 9},
        {1611, "Grobbulus", [[ One of the failed creations of an army of flesh giants, Grobbulus dwells in the Abomination Quarter at Naxxramas. A terrifying monster created by the Scourge's army. The product of the twisted minds of the Scourge's engineers and brilliant surgeons. This enormous walking mutagen is steeped in poison, death, fear, and drool... repugnant drool. ]], 0.615762, 0.531547, 1, 535, 11626, 754, 3, 0, 10},
        {1612, "Gluth", [[ This enormous undead hound, which devours surplus zombies, resides at Naxxramas. Countless corpses, devoured by this monster, have granted it a supernatural unholy power. It now resides in a sealed-off part of the Abomination Quarter at Naxxramas, and the only way to reach it is through the sewers. ]], 0.462924, 0.438272, 1, 535, 11633, 754, 3, 0, 11},
        {1613, "Thaddius", [[ A monstrous flesh giant, in which tormented, agonized souls still calling for help are sealed, it resides in the Abomination Quarter at Naxxramas. Necromancy and experiments with electricity have made this monster undead, and woe to anyone who faces a creature capable of reducing its enemies to ash with a bolt of lightning. ]], 0.265857, 0.145792, 1, 535, 11639, 754, 3, 0, 12},
        {1614, "Sapphiron", [[ Once a powerful servant of Malygos, keeper of artifacts and an undefeated dragon of the blue flight, Sapphiron confronted Arthas during his journey to the Frozen Throne, and was defeated. Arthas then sacrificed a significant portion of his power at the time to resurrect Sapphiron in the form of a mighty frost wyrm, and with his help managed to breach the defenses of Azjol-Nerub. Today, this dragon guards Kel'Thuzad's chambers, in the Frost Wyrm's Lair, in the Upper Necropolis of Naxxramas. ]], 0.565133, 0.675014, 6, 535, 11652, 754, 3, 0, 13},
        {1615, "Kel'Thuzad", [[ Kel'Thuzad is one of the chief servants of the Lich King, responsible for spreading the Scourge's plague across Lordaeron. After being killed by Arthas during the Third War, he was reborn as a lich. With Arthas's help, he summoned Archimonde the Defiler, leader of the Burning Legion. Nevertheless, Kel'Thuzad was truly devoted to the Lich King, not to the Burning Legion. When Arthas departed for Northrend at the time of the events surrounding the Frozen Throne, he left Kel'Thuzad as regent to command the Scourge in Lordaeron. Previously, he ruled the Plaguelands from the necropolis of Naxxramas, hovering above Stratholme, but today, Naxxramas and Kel'Thuzad along with it are located in the eastern part of Icecrown, where he once again serves the Lich King. ]], 0.365324, 0.223293, 6, 535, 11660, 754, 3, 0, 14},
    },
    [755] = {
        {1616, "Sartharion", [[ Guardian of the Obsidian Sanctum, whose mission is to protect the brood of Deathwing's new generation. ]], 0.505736, 0.477055, 0, 531, 11419, 755, 3, 0, 0},
    },
    [756] = {
        {1617, "Malygos", [[ Malygos, the Guardian of Magic, driven mad by grief and pain, has declared war on all who use magic, seeing in mages nothing but a source of chaos and disaster. In the Eye of Eternity, within the Nexus, he gathers the energy of Azeroth's ley lines, determined to put an end, once and for all, to the threat of excessive magic use. Your goal is to stop him. ]], 0.384321, 0.498566, 1, 527, 11449, 756, 3, 0, 0},
    },
    [757] = {
        {1618, "Gormok the Impaler", [[  ]], 0.511514, 0.527373, 1, 543, 2450, 757, -1, 0, 0},
        {1619, "Lord Jaraxxus", [[  ]], 0.463713, 0.405480, 1, 543, 11000, 757, -1, 0, 1},
        {1620, "Alyssia Moonstalker", [[ The Alliance demands justice and challenges you, champions of the Horde. Your opponents will be among the finest warriors of the Alliance who took part in this tournament, but those who have defied the Horde will fall. Lok'tar ogar! ]], 0.428340, 0.527373, 1, 543, 11059, 757, -1, 8, 2},
        {1621, "Birana Stormhoof", [[ The Horde has dared accuse the Alliance of conspiring to summon an eredar lord, and now demands justice, challenging you, champions of the Alliance. Your opponents will be the fiercest and most skilled warriors of the Horde, but they are no match for you, and must be annihilated. Glory to the Alliance! ]], 0.428340, 0.527373, 1, 543, 11201, 757, -1, 4, 2},
        {1622, "Fjola Lightbane", [[  ]], 0.463713, 0.649266, 1, 543, 11016, 757, -1, 0, 3},
        {1623, "Anub'arak", [[  ]], 0.532546, 0.355289, 2, 543, 11038, 757, -1, 0, 4},
    },
    [758] = {
        {1624, "Lord Marrowgar", [[ The Lich King created Marrowgar from the bones of thousands of vanished adventurers, and he now guards the Frozen Throne at the foot of the Spire, empowered by the very might of the throne itself. ]], 0.391055, 0.593338, 1, 604, 11677, 758, -1, 0, 0},
        {1625, "Lady Deathwhisper", [[ Lady Deathwhisper permanently replaced Kel'Thuzad after the fall of Naxxramas, becoming the true ruler of the Cult of the Damned. At Icecrown Citadel, she trains the cult's most gifted and ambitious devotees, preparing a new magical guard for the Scourge. ]], 0.391055, 0.869980, 1, 604, 11683, 758, -1, 0, 1},
        {1626, "High Overlord Saurfang", [[  ]], 0.219927, 0.550191, 2, 604, 0, 758, -1, 4, 2},
        {1627, "Muradin Bronzebeard", [[  ]], 0.690500, 0.550191, 2, 604, 0, 758, -1, 8, 2},
        {1628, "Deathbringer Saurfang", [[ This brave and powerful orc, fallen beneath the Lich King's blows at the Wrath Gate, was turned into a death knight and now guards the entrance to the inner sanctum of Icecrown Citadel. The Lich King granted him a special power: Saurfang's blood possesses an incredible healing effect, allowing him alone to hold off an entire army, fighting on to victory. ]], 0.515422, 0.216060, 0, 604, 11713, 758, -1, 0, 3},
        {1629, "Stinky", [[ One of two giant abominations created by Festergut. Endowed with considerable physical strength and wielding foul putrid gas, Stinky is a dangerous weapon of the Scourge. ]], 0.198978, 0.654874, 0, 604, 11726, 758, -1, 0, 4},
        {1630, "Precious", [[ Professor Putricide's favorite creature. This abomination, oozing corrosive drool and sometimes animated, endowed with considerable physical strength, Precious is a dangerous weapon of the Scourge. ]], 0.198978, 0.418259, 0, 604, 11733, 758, -1, 0, 5},
        {1631, "Professor Putricide", [[ It is sometimes said that genius borders on madness. Professor Putricide is a striking example. A mad genius who has created numerous types of plague, creator of abominations, greatest alchemist of all time, Putricide resides in the Plague Factory at Icecrown Citadel, and his ingenuity knows no bounds. ]], 0.131101, 0.532982, 0, 604, 11747, 758, -1, 0, 6},
        {1632, "Prince Valanar", [[ Valanar, Keleseth, and Taldaram, the Kindred, three blood princes defeated by the heroes of Azeroth, former blood elves who traded the power of the Sunwell for that of blood. Their bodies have been carefully preserved and brought to the Crimson Hall of Icecrown Citadel, where they are destined to be resurrected and continue their eternal service. ]], 0.520160, 0.141491, 0, 604, 11779, 758, -1, 0, 7},
        {1633, "Blood-Queen Lana'thel", [[ During the battles across the icy wastes of Northrend, Arthas won victory over Illidan and Kael'thas, and the few survivors tried to escape the Scourge. But the Lich King was determined to hunt down every elf who had dared defy him. Cornered, Lana'thel desperately attacked Arthas, but could not withstand Frostmourne.

The Lich King resurrected Lana'thel and made her leader of the Kindred, the blood elves who oversaw the Scourge's operations across the entire northern continent. Today, Lana'thel resides in the Crimson Hall of Icecrown Citadel, and her power fuels the seal leading to the teleporter atop the Frozen Throne. ]], 0.511599, 0.435467, 0, 604, 11792, 758, -1, 0, 8},
        {1634, "Valithria Dreamwalker", [[ One of Ysera's daughters, a powerful dragon fallen into the Scourge's hands. Imprisoned deep within the Frostwing Halls at Icecrown Citadel, Valithria is being tortured and will likely not be left alive should any chance of freedom arise. Help her before it's too late! ]], 0.766814, 0.736678, 0, 604, 11808, 758, -1, 0, 9},
        {1635, "Sindragosa", [[ Sensing her death approaching, blinded, Sindragosa wished for only one thing: to reach the Dragon Wastes and find death there, as so many dragons before her had. But the dragon's strength did not last much longer. Exhausted, she collapsed upon the ice of Icecrown. In one last effort, with a cry filled with despair, Sindragosa called out to her mate Malygos. Only the freezing Arctic winds answered her. But she did not give up and called out a second time. The distance was too great. Understanding that her soul would never find rest at the Dragon Wastes, she resigned herself to her fate. Life slowly left her, and her mind grew clouded.

In her delirium, her final thoughts were filled with disappointment and hatred: hatred for the Legion, hatred for Neltharion, and even hatred for Malygos. But it was the world of mortals she hated most...

And before dying, Sindragosa swore vengeance.

The place where this mighty dragon met her death came to be called Sindragosa's Fall.

Such was the fate of this blue dragon. However, as we all know, the story does not end there. Thousands of years later, the mighty Lich King found Sindragosa and offered her the chance to fulfill her mortal oath. He made her queen of the frost dragons and installed her in the Frostwing Halls. Today, Sindragosa carries out Arthas's orders. In the Pit of Saron, you witnessed her current power with your own eyes. ]], 0.366325, 0.231898, 0, 604, 11829, 758, -1, 0, 10},
        {1636, "The Lich King", [[ After his awakening, the Lich King hastened first to tear out his own heart, believing that anything tying him to mortals made him weaker. He traveled to Sindragosa's Fall and resurrected the ancient dragon Sindragosa, Malygos's first mate, in the form of a frost wyrm. He then reviewed his gigantic undead army, ready for war. During his sleep, the death knights trained across the lands of Icecrown. Upon waking, he ordered them to march on the Chapel of the Damned, where thousands of Alliance heroes lay at rest, each destined to be resurrected into his service, before conquering these lands for the Scourge. Today he sits upon the Frozen Throne, in Icecrown Citadel, and only his death can stop the Scourge's war machine before it annihilates all life. ]], 0.499296, 0.528743, 0, 604, 11855, 758, -1, 0, 11},
        {1637, "Lady Jaina Proudmoore", [[ Atop Icecrown Citadel, a moment before the Lich King was to receive a killing blow, the history of this world changed. Lady Jaina Proudmoore cast aside the voice of reason and stood to defend the one she had once loved so dearly. Arthas's fate now rests on whether the heroes of Azeroth can strike down, not an incarnation of evil, but a lost companion. ]], 0.499296, 0.568743, 0, 604, 900, 758, 8, 0, 12},
    },
    [760] = {
        {1651, "Onyxia", [[ At the edge of the Swamp of Sorrows stands a cave that has become the last refuge of the cursed black dragonflight's bloodline. Onyxia's Lair is the name of this refuge, and the number of black dragons within grows slowly but surely with each passing day. This threat cannot be ignored. ]], 0.672370, 0.309886, 0, 718, 11400, 760, 3, 0, 0},
    },
    [761] = {
        {1652, "Halion", [[  ]], 0.491354, 0.535788, 0, 609, 1000, 761, -1, 0, 0},
    },
    [762] = {
        {11585, "Oggleflint", [[ Oggleflint and the troggs once ruled unchallenged over the depths of the Burning Steppes, until the Burning Blade cultists made their appearance. Too weak to drive off the Burning Blade, Oggleflint and the troggs retreated to the upper levels of the Wailing Caverns... wait, of Blackrock Depths, where they now wait patiently for this unwelcome guest. ]], 0.566000, 0.385000, 0, 680, 20001, 762, -1, 0, 1},
        {11586, "Taragaman the Hungerer", [[ He is considered the leader of the Burning Blade; he hides in the fiery depths of Blackrock Depths, using his demonic influence to corrupt the citizens of Orgrimmar. In reality, the true leaders of the Burning Blade are Bazzalan and Jergosh, this fel guardian being nothing more than an expendable decoy to lure young Horde adventurers to their deaths. ]], 0.410000, 0.574000, 0, 680, 20002, 762, -1, 0, 2},
        {11587, "Bazzalan", [[ Bazzalan leads the Burning Blade cultists alongside Jergosh the Invoker. His motives remain unclear, but like all satyrs, he is a swift and cunning opponent. ]], 0.420000, 0.861000, 0, 680, 20004, 762, -1, 0, 3},
        {11588, "Jergosh the Invoker", [[ Jergosh the Invoker has renounced the ideals of the orcs and practices the dark, demonic arts of the warlock. Leader of the Burning Blade cultists, Jergosh resides in Blackrock Depths, plotting a scheme dangerous enough to draw the attention of Thrall himself. He guards a sphere filled with blood, needed to summon the most dangerous demons. ]], 0.343000, 0.817000, 0, 680, 20006, 762, -1, 0, 7},
    },
    [763] = {
        {11589, "Interrogator Vishas", [[ James Vishas is a Scarlet Crusader and the order's chief interrogator. He enjoys torturing any undead he captures and takes great pride in his work. Vishas is known for his relentless sadism, his cruel experiments, and his shrill voice. Interrogator Vishas tortured Vorrel Sengutz for weeks. Vishas took Sengutz's engagement ring and gave it to his own wife, Nancy Vishas. Nancy lives with Vishas's grandfather, presumably James's father though this is never mentioned, in a cottage on the eastern shore of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. ]], 0.719000, 0.594000, 0, 889, 20272, 763, -1, 0, 1},
        {11590, "Ironspine", [[ Ironspine is a rare elite level 31 skeleton dwelling in the graveyard of the Scarlet Monastery. Lanky and seemingly fragile, these skeletons possess superhuman strength and high resistance to most physical attacks. ]], 0.517000, 0.675000, 0, 889, 20274, 763, -1, 0, 1},
        {11591, "Fallen Champion", [[ Once a holy paladin of the Scarlet Monastery, the Fallen Champion was a hero of the Scarlet Crusade, later killed and raised in service to the Lich King. He wanders the graveyard still wearing the armor and wielding the weapon he used in life, but since the undead cannot wield the powers of the holy Light, he has become a warrior instead. ]], 0.355000, 0.664000, 0, 889, 20276, 763, -1, 0, 1},
        {11592, "Bloodmage Thalnos", [[ Bloodmage Thalnos is an elite skeletal mini-boss found in the graveyard of the Scarlet Monastery, just beneath the stairs at the far end of the cemetery. ]], 0.243000, 0.560000, 0, 889, 20278, 763, -1, 0, 1},
    },
    [764] = {
        {11593, "High Inquisitor Fairbanks", [[ Fairbanks was a trusted advisor to Highlord Mograine and attended the meeting at Southshore that led to the creation of the Ashbringer.

Fairbanks and Highlord Mograine were betrayed by Mograine's own son, Renault, at Deathknell, where legions of the Scourge lay in wait. Fairbanks was the first to fall, but did not die, trapped and hidden beneath the corpses of the undead. He silently witnessed Renault's betrayal, hearing Mograine's anguished screams as the Ashbringer pierced his heart and grazed its blade. Kel'Thuzad later raised Mograine as a death knight.

Back at the Scarlet Monastery, Fairbanks told this story of betrayal to anyone willing to listen. Those who believed him left the Crusade to found the Argent Dawn. Fairbanks was later killed by the remaining crusaders for blasphemy and, no doubt, for showing symptoms of the plague. His body was thrown into a secret room in the cathedral of the Scarlet Monastery. ]], 0.553000, 0.256000, 0, 940, 20282, 764, -1, 0, 1},
        {11594, "Scarlet Commander Mograine", [[ Scarlet Commander Mograine is a young commander of the Scarlet Crusade's armed forces at the Scarlet Monastery. He is an elite boss, a level 40 paladin, found in the Crusaders' Chapel within the Scarlet Monastery's cathedral. ]], 0.492000, 0.271000, 0, 940, 20288, 764, -1, 0, 1},
        {11595, "High Inquisitor Whitehead", [[ Sally Whitemane is a priestess of the Light and High Inquisitor of the Scarlet Crusade. She directs their activities from the cathedral of the Scarlet Monastery. Still young, Sally witnessed her family's death, claimed by the terrible undead plague. Since that day, this feared priestess has found satisfaction and pleasure in only one thing: purifying and destroying the undead. ]], 0.490000, 0.168000, 0, 940, 20292, 764, -1, 0, 1},
    },
    [765] = {
        {11596, "Houndmaster Loksey", [[ Houndmaster Loksey is one of four leaders of the Scarlet Monastery and the captain responsible for training the hounds the Scarlet Crusade uses to track down its enemies. Loksey commands fearsome hounds capable of shredding their prey in mere minutes. ]], 0.293000, 0.837000, 0, 938, 20298, 765, -1, 0, 1},
        {11597, "Arcanist Doan", [[ He is the guardian of the monastery's library, keeper of a secret that even the Scarlet Crusade itself is said to distrust. He nonetheless remains a trusted man of the Crusade, holding a vital key granting access to the Scarlet Crusade's operations in the Plaguelands. The sorcerer Doan is convinced that arcane magic is the only way to free Lordaeron from the Scourge. ]], 0.833000, 0.742000, 0, 938, 20300, 765, -1, 0, 1},
    },
    [766] = {
        {11598, "Herod", [[ The Scarlet Crusade possesses a vast arsenal of tools to fight the undead. Novices must first learn to wield blades and hammers, arrows and shields. Herod has devoted his entire life to the art of combat with these destructive instruments, and he is more than eager to demonstrate his skill to the order's unholy enemies. ]], 0.786000, 0.104000, 0, 939, 20305, 766, -1, 0, 1},
    },
    [767] = {
        {11599, "Kirtonos the Herald", [[ He has long been a master of Scholomance. Responsible for numerous atrocities during Krastinov's rule over the school, Kirtonos fed on the blood of his innocent victims. To appease his master, Doctor Krastinov had to supply him with ever-increasing quantities of blood. ]], 0.497000, 0.101000, 2, 890, 20309, 767, -1, 0, 0},
        {11600, "Jandice Barov", [[ Jandice Barov is a human ghost, a mini-boss found within Scholomance, in a secret room. She is a member of the unfortunate Barov family. It was an extremely wealthy family from Lordaeron, owner of lands including Caer Darrow and many others. ]], 0.541000, 0.144000, 3, 890, 20317, 767, -1, 0, 1},
        {11601, "Rattlegore", [[ Rattlegore is a bone golem boss in Scholomance. After being defeated by the Alliance during the Battle of Andorhal, he was recreated from bones within Scholomance, in the main crypt. ]], 0.321000, 0.650000, 3, 890, 20319, 767, -1, 0, 2},
        {11602, "Ras Frostwhisper", [[ Ras Frostwhisper is a lich of the Scourge and overseer of everything that happens in Scholomance. He observed and trained all who rose to the rank of Master of Darkness. He was Kel'Thuzad's lieutenant and favorite student. Ras Frostwhisper was once a human mage from Strahnbrad. He was a wild mage, a rogue sorcerer who never received formal training in Dalaran. ]], 0.405000, 0.815000, 4, 890, 20322, 767, -1, 0, 5},
        {11603, "Doctor Theolen Krastinov", [[ Nicknamed 'the Butcher,' Krastinov was the servant of Kirtonos the Herald, as well as chief torturer and supplier of bodies and body parts for the necromantic experiments of Scholomance. His first victims were recruited from the Caer Darrow family. ]], 0.888000, 0.462000, 3, 890, 20328, 767, -1, 0, 7},
        {11604, "Marduk Blackpool", [[ Marduk Blackpool, also known as Marduk the Black, was an infamous death knight of the Scourge. He is notably known for his role in the Battle of Shadeglen during the Third War, where he sealed the humans' defeat by corrupting the mind of Joseph Redpath. Some time later, Marduk withdrew into Scholomance. ]], 0.442000, 0.644000, 2, 890, 20331, 767, -1, 0, 3},
        {11605, "Vectus", [[ Vectus is a skeletal mage mini-boss and one of the chief instructors of necromancy at Scholomance. Vectus has raised a brood of tortured dragons dwelling in Scholomance, which he obtained by paying Tinkey Steamboil, in the Burning Steppes, for eggs from Blackrock Mountain. ]], 0.486000, 0.658000, 2, 890, 20335, 767, -1, 0, 4},
        {11606, "Lorekeeper Polkelt", [[ Polkelt is one of six mini-bosses required to summon Gandling. As his name suggests, he was once a keeper of lore, sadly now lost, since he is nothing more today than a clumsy, mindless monster. ]], 0.723000, 0.220000, 3, 890, 20339, 767, -1, 0, 8},
        {11607, "Instructor Malicia", [[ Instructor Malicia is a high elf instructor who trains the cultists of Scholomance. ]], 0.726000, 0.700000, 3, 890, 20343, 767, -1, 0, 6},
        {11608, "Lady Illucia Barov", [[ Lady Illucia Barov is a ghost mini-boss found within Scholomance. She was the wife of Lord Alexei Barov and one of six mini-bosses that must be defeated to summon the Dark Master Gandling. ]], 0.675000, 0.141000, 4, 890, 20348, 767, -1, 0, 11},
        {11609, "Lord Alexei Barov", [[ Lord Alexei Barov was lord of Caer Darrow, Brill, Tarren Mill, and Southshore. He was the father of Alexi, Weldon, and Jandice Barov, and the husband of Lady Illucia Barov. Like Jandice and Illucia, he is now an agent of the Scourge within Scholomance. Alexei Barov is one of six bosses that must be defeated to summon the Dark Master Gandling. He also keeps the deeds of ownership to Caer Darrow. ]], 0.791000, 0.300000, 4, 890, 20353, 767, -1, 0, 10},
        {11610, "The Ravenian", [[ Raven'ian is an unusual type of undead. It is unknown how this transformation took place. Rumor has it that Raven'ian devours the students of Scholomance who fail to show enough diligence in their studies. In addition, Raven'ian is one of six bosses that must be defeated to summon the Dark Master Gandling. ]], 0.673000, 0.477000, 4, 890, 20356, 767, -1, 0, 9},
        {11611, "Dark Master Gandling", [[ Dark Master Gandling is the final boss of Scholomance. His necromancy instructor was Ras Frostwhisper. Gandling is the headmaster of the School of Necromancy at Caer Darrow, personally appointed by Kel'Thuzad. ]], 0.681000, 0.302000, 4, 890, 20360, 767, -1, 0, 12},
    },
    [771] = {
        {11623, "Leviathan Defense Turret", [[ The entrance to Ulduar's inner courtyard is guarded by an enormous armored tank. Keeper Mimiron built the 'Flame Leviathan' as part of the 'V-0-7 TR0N' weapons platform. ]], 0.491000, 0.389000, 1, 529, 20484, 771, -1, 0, 0},
        {11624, "Ignis the Furnace Master", [[ Like other titan constructs of Ulduar, Ignis now serves the will of the Old God Yogg-Saron. This towering fire giant resides in the Great Forge and creates armies of iron warriors meant to conquer Azeroth, in Yogg-Saron's name. ]], 0.383000, 0.266000, 1, 529, 20534, 771, -1, 0, 1},
        {11625, "Razorscale", [[ Veranus, mother of the proto-dragon brood of Storm Peaks, served Keeper Thorim until Loken captured her and turned her into a fearsome weapon. Furnace Master Ignis reinforced the dragon's scales with plates of iron, making Razorscale even deadlier. ]], 0.541000, 0.268000, 1, 529, 20545, 771, -1, 0, 2},
        {11626, "XT-002 Deconstructor", [[ Mimiron designed this autonomous mechanism to guard Ulduar's scrapyard and gave it just enough rudimentary intelligence to carry out simple tasks. XT-002 considers itself the Keeper's son and, like a moody child, sometimes throws tantrums. ]], 0.485000, 0.145000, 1, 529, 20566, 771, -1, 0, 3},
        {11627, "Steelbreaker", [[ At the head of Loken's iron legions stand three fearsome generals, each representing one of the races created by the titans. Bouraq Stormfront, Molgeim the Runemaster, and the giant Steelbreaker serve the one who truly commands the Keeper: the sinister Yogg-Saron. ]], 0.154000, 0.568000, 2, 529, 20587, 771, -1, 0, 4},
        {11628, "Kologarn", [[ Loken ordered Furnace Master Ignis to forge this giant to defend the Shattered Walkway. With his immense hands, Kologarn is able to crush anyone who tries to infiltrate the inner sanctum of Ulduar. ]], 0.373000, 0.126000, 2, 529, 20607, 771, -1, 0, 5},
        {11629, "Auriaya", [[ Ulduar's archivist roams the Watchers' Circle accompanied by wild cats. Long years spent in solitude have broken Auriaya, and the growing influence of the Old God has finally driven her to complete madness. ]], 0.511000, 0.569000, 3, 529, 20619, 771, -1, 0, 6},
        {11630, "Hodir", [[ Hodir once ruled over the Temple of Winter, commanding the snow giants of Storm Peaks. Today, this Keeper resides in an icy cave within the Halls of Winter, his mind bent to the will of Yogg-Saron. ]], 0.667000, 0.637000, 3, 529, 20632, 771, -1, 0, 7},
        {11631, "Thorim", [[ For years, Thorim believed that giants had killed his beloved wife Sif. Unleashing his wrath on his allies, he sank into despair. When Thorim discovered that his brother Loken was behind this crime, Loken imprisoned him within Ulduar, where the Old God clouded his mind. ]], 0.718000, 0.484000, 3, 529, 20656, 771, -1, 0, 8},
        {11632, "Freya", [[ Keeper Freya was the protector of all life, aided in this task by three loyal ancients. And though her garden continues to be strangled by unchecked growth, her sanity did not withstand the whispers of the Old God. ]], 0.533000, 0.230000, 3, 529, 20711, 771, -1, 0, 9},
        {11633, "VX-001", [[ A brilliant inventor, Mimiron designed many mechanisms throughout Azeroth's history that still inspire awe and wonder today. But having fallen under Loken's influence, this Keeper of Ulduar now creates nothing but machines of war. ]], 0.436000, 0.414000, 5, 529, 20752, 771, -1, 0, 10},
        {11634, "General Vezax", [[ Strange creatures called the faceless ones dwell in the depths of Ulduar. One of their lords, General Vezax, guards the winding corridors that lead to Yogg-Saron's prison. ]], 0.569000, 0.605000, 4, 529, 20793, 771, -1, 0, 11},
        {11635, "Yogg-Saron", [[ A waking dream, a monster from your nightmares, a demon with a thousand faces.
All must bow before the master's will. Your feeble efforts only make him stronger... ]], 0.681000, 0.401000, 4, 529, 20805, 771, -1, 0, 12},
        {11636, "Algalon the Observer", [[ After Loken's death, a warning was sent to the Pantheon that Azeroth had lost its Chief Custodian. Shortly after, Algalon the Observer arrived on Azeroth, tasked with detecting signs of the planet's corruption. If necessary, the Worldstar would trigger the world's Reorigination algorithm, resulting in the death of all its inhabitants. ]], 0.788000, 0.466000, 2, 529, 20863, 771, -1, 0, 13},
    },
    [773] = {
        {11657, "Earthrager Shaman", [[ The first of Murozond's honor guard, a powerful warrior who fights fiercely in melee and wields destructive temporal magic, reducing his foes to dust. ]], 0.661000, 0.648000, 0, 924, 21202, 773, 10, 0, 1},
        {11658, "Eoin's Infused Tankard", [[ The greatest of Murozond's chronomancers, tasked by him with guarding one of the two passages leading out of time. A powerful spellcaster, he does not pursue his enemies, preferring to bombard them with spells until they engage him in melee themselves. ]], 0.718000, 0.848000, 0, 924, 21215, 773, 10, 0, 2},
        {11659, "Bronze-Beak Griffin", [[ Every soul harbors a share of darkness and madness. Nozdormu's spirit, once noble and devoted to his duty, was consumed by the vision of his own death, granted to him by Aman'Thul. He is now Murozond, lord of the Infinite dragonflight, having turned against his own destiny and determined to survive at any cost, even if it means causing the End of Time and the end of the world as we know it.
Here, in this dying timeline, his labors have clearly borne fruit, and only one final step remains: erase this timeline... then move on to the next. ]], 0.376000, 0.249000, 0, 924, 21238, 773, 10, 0, 3},
    },
    [774] = {
        {11660, "Gogonas", [[ Unable to hold the immense pit lord Argaloth in the majestic dungeons of Dalaran's Violet Hold, the mages of the Kirin Tor were forced to lock this powerful demon in one of the strongest prisons: the depths of Tol Barad. Unfortunately, or fortunately, the guards could not long withstand the burning hatred radiating from the demon, and in an attempt to end his existence, the demon broke free. ]], 0.802000, 0.627000, 0, 954, 21288, 774, 3, 0, 0},
        {11661, "Mindsucker Ktrax", [[ This fearsome creature was captured in the depths of Ulduar. It was trapped as it sank into a stupor after Yogg-Saron's defeat. Fearing its power, the mages of the Kirin Tor decided to send it to an ultra-secure location: the Tol Barad prison; however, over time, the creature has mysteriously awakened, and the powerful security systems of Tol Barad can no longer contain it. ]], 0.478000, 0.175000, 0, 954, 21298, 774, 3, 0, 1},
        {11662, "Magic Eater", [[ Brought in still a 'pup,' the devourer slowly but surely grew in the depths of Tol Barad, until practitioners of Shadow and Fel magic settled nearby. The magic they radiated gradually seeped into the devourer's still-weak body, altering and transforming its essence. ]], 0.162000, 0.631000, 0, 954, 21322, 774, 3, 0, 2},
    },
    [777] = {
        {11672, "Primal Devilsaur", [[ Much blood has been spilled in the struggle between the Alliance, the Horde, and the Renegades over the resources and treasures of Tol Barad. Drop by drop, the blood reached the ley line at the very heart of the island, deep underground, and the blood found an echo. With a groan, the prison gates opened, and the now-accessible passage calls out to treasure hunters of every faction. Only one obstacle remains: the Guardian of the Ley Lines, Norgorn, awakened by the call of blood. ]], 0.162000, 0.631000, 0, 0, 21530, 777, 1, 0, 0},
    },
}
